So then he's like...

2280
01:28:55.606 --> 01:28:56.449
Well, because

2281
01:28:56.449 --> 01:28:58.748
and I'm sure we'll get to 101 pretty quick here,

2282
01:28:58.748 --> 01:29:01.794
but we didn't make the decision to do 101

2283
01:29:01.794 --> 01:29:05.444
until that Sunday, the final decision, so three days before.

2284
01:29:05.444 --> 01:29:06.398
And when I had talked to you on that-

2285
01:29:06.398 --> 01:29:08.307
You had the shirts made up and everything.

2286
01:29:08.307 --> 01:29:09.140
In 48 hours.

2287
01:29:09.140 --> 01:29:09.973
Oh, you did, wow.

2288
01:29:09.973 --> 01:29:11.651
And they were hand delivered.

2289
01:29:11.651 --> 01:29:13.370
Yeah, it's crazy.

2290
01:29:13.370 --> 01:29:16.640
And people think it was planned because we had the jersey,

2291
01:29:16.640 --> 01:29:17.535
but that was a-

2292
01:29:17.535 --> 01:29:18.913
It was like how'd did you get that jersey?

2293
01:29:18.913 --> 01:29:20.514
We're like, we don't know.
We don't know.

2294
01:29:20.514 --> 01:29:24.281
It literally hand delivered in two days.

2295
01:29:24.281 --> 01:29:26.567
Well, when we had that conversation on day 21,

2296
01:29:26.567 --> 01:29:29.303
I mean on day 91, I was being super patient,

2297
01:29:29.303 --> 01:29:31.227
my shin was healing, I didn't have any pain,

2298
01:29:31.227 --> 01:29:32.821
I was on the other side of the hip,

2299
01:29:32.821 --> 01:29:37.635
I was just like, I am going to run that last day.

2300
01:29:37.635 --> 01:29:39.082
And right from the go, I started to run

2301
01:29:39.082 --> 01:29:41.665
and I got to, I was so excited,

2302
01:29:42.630 --> 01:29:44.391
but I knew things started to go south

2303
01:29:44.391 --> 01:29:47.564
because I had already I mean, obviously asked

2304
01:29:47.564 --> 01:29:49.945
so much from my body and my mind.

2305
01:29:49.945 --> 01:29:53.107
I mean, we're at the very tail end of a quarter of a year,

2306
01:29:53.107 --> 01:29:56.517
had done something nobody thought was physically possible.

2307
01:29:56.517 --> 01:29:59.878
And I had just really nursed my body back to health

2308
01:29:59.878 --> 01:30:04.215
in the midst of so much trauma and so much stress

2309
01:30:04.215 --> 01:30:06.628
and I made it all the way to 19, Rich.

2310
01:30:06.628 --> 01:30:08.298
I made it to mile 19 running.

2311
01:30:08.298 --> 01:30:10.898
And then, like you said,

2312
01:30:10.898 --> 01:30:13.187
if things went sideways in the beginning of the campaign,

2313
01:30:13.187 --> 01:30:16.714
they went sideways on day 100 and day 19.

2314
01:30:16.714 --> 01:30:19.381
And I don't remember a lot of it

2315
01:30:20.973 --> 01:30:22.775
because I had to check out

2316
01:30:22.775 --> 01:30:26.734
and I just remember the wing men were there

2317
01:30:26.734 --> 01:30:28.088
and Felicia was there.

2318
01:30:28.088 --> 01:30:30.684
Our 110 pound friend who'd be the one to catch him.

2319
01:30:30.684 --> 01:30:33.223
And I just remember, I'd manage it, manage it

2320
01:30:33.223 --> 01:30:35.223
and then my legs just...

2321
01:30:36.112 --> 01:30:38.210
I had asked everything out of them

2322
01:30:38.210 --> 01:30:40.602
and they would give out on me

2323
01:30:40.602 --> 01:30:43.217
and the collapsed moments,

2324
01:30:43.217 --> 01:30:47.013
but I had gave me the 30 seconds to recoup

2325
01:30:47.013 --> 01:30:50.522
and mentally we had a mantra and it was here we go

2326
01:30:50.522 --> 01:30:53.376
and when you said, here we go, we start moving again.

2327
01:30:53.376 --> 01:30:57.506
And I remember we were on the last Out N Back

2328
01:30:57.506 --> 01:30:58.672
headed up to 8th North

2329
01:30:58.672 --> 01:31:00.818
and we probably had three miles to go,

2330
01:31:00.818 --> 01:31:03.639
it was after 19, I'd fallen apart.

2331
01:31:03.639 --> 01:31:07.056
I had lost my goal to run the whole thing

2332
01:31:08.244 --> 01:31:11.333
'cause my legs kept giving out on me

2333
01:31:11.333 --> 01:31:15.575
and we were probably mile 22 or 23 and I lost it again

2334
01:31:15.575 --> 01:31:18.208
and Felicia caught me.

2335
01:31:18.208 --> 01:31:20.625
And right before I went down,

2336
01:31:21.497 --> 01:31:23.137
I was looking at my watch and I said,

2337
01:31:23.137 --> 01:31:24.356
how fast are we running?

2338
01:31:24.356 --> 01:31:27.523
And she's like, we're running at 9:30.

2339
01:31:28.845 --> 01:31:30.933
And then my legs gave out and I collapsed again

2340
01:31:30.933 --> 01:31:32.232
and then I got back up and I said,

2341
01:31:32.232 --> 01:31:34.433
I can do better than this.

2342
01:31:34.433 --> 01:31:36.016
And her jaw dropped

2343
01:31:37.620 --> 01:31:41.101
because she's like, you're on day 100

2344
01:31:41.101 --> 01:31:43.390
of 100 consecutive Ironmans.

2345
01:31:43.390 --> 01:31:46.013
You have given everything you got,

2346
01:31:46.013 --> 01:31:49.025
you've given everything you've had or had

2347
01:31:49.025 --> 01:31:53.376
and your mindset right now is I can do better than this.

2348
01:31:53.376 --> 01:31:55.017
And that's truly where my mind was

2349
01:31:55.017 --> 01:31:57.017
because you wanna go out

2350
01:32:01.899 --> 01:32:04.941
kind of with a bang, like we did on the 50.

2351
01:32:04.941 --> 01:32:09.058
And I had been dreaming of it for a long time on that run

2352
01:32:09.058 --> 01:32:10.884
and being so patient, allowing my body,

2353
01:32:10.884 --> 01:32:13.742
and I've obviously asked a lot for my body,

2354
01:32:13.742 --> 01:32:17.373
but it was kind of that moment where

2355
01:32:17.373 --> 01:32:22.208
like it was a proud moment for me because I was at the end,

2356
01:32:22.208 --> 01:32:26.358
but my mind was still there from my perspective,

2357
01:32:26.358 --> 01:32:30.858
and even in that moment, I knew I could do or be more.

2358
01:32:31.988 --> 01:32:36.525
For people that don't know, I mean, in the final miles,

2359
01:32:36.525 --> 01:32:37.790
you were literally collapsing,

2360
01:32:37.790 --> 01:32:40.322
you were passing out and people had to catch you.

2361
01:32:40.322 --> 01:32:42.517
Did you ever fall all the way down to the pavement?

2362
01:32:42.517 --> 01:32:43.691
I didn't,

2363
01:32:43.691 --> 01:32:47.527
and it's crazy 'cause I've seen pictures now

2364
01:32:47.527 --> 01:32:49.225
where it was bad.
It was bad.

2365
01:32:49.225 --> 01:32:51.565
And I've seen pictures now where like Casey and Aaron

2366
01:32:51.565 --> 01:32:53.315
are like right there.

2367
01:32:54.177 --> 01:32:56.505
Any stumble or anything that I do,

2368
01:32:56.505 --> 01:32:58.469
they are right there anticipating it.

2369
01:32:58.469 --> 01:33:01.939
And I wouldn't have made it the last day without them

2370
01:33:01.939 --> 01:33:04.067
just because of the pace that we're pushing,

2371
01:33:04.067 --> 01:33:08.551
we'd done five hours on the bike course, which is moving.

2372
01:33:08.551 --> 01:33:13.426
And so I'd asked a lot from my body just on that bike ride,

2373
01:33:13.426 --> 01:33:16.289
knowing it was the last day, but also knowing...

2374
01:33:16.289 --> 01:33:20.372
We didn't wanna let on that we were gonna do 101,

2375
01:33:21.418 --> 01:33:22.423
and I had been telling people

2376
01:33:22.423 --> 01:33:24.689
on social media the whole time,

2377
01:33:24.689 --> 01:33:27.083
I'm gonna run 100, brace yourself.

2378
01:33:27.083 --> 01:33:29.648
If you plan to join me that day, we're moving,

2379
01:33:29.648 --> 01:33:31.815
we're gonna go sub 12, 11,

2380
01:33:33.601 --> 01:33:36.294
and then things fell apart.

2381
01:33:36.294 --> 01:33:38.017
But at the back of my mind, I said,

2382
01:33:38.017 --> 01:33:38.993
okay, I can't allude

2383
01:33:38.993 --> 01:33:41.572
to the fact that I got to get up and do this again tomorrow.

2384
01:33:41.572 --> 01:33:43.576
So even after I broke myself

2385
01:33:43.576 --> 01:33:45.655
and drove myself into the ground,

2386
01:33:45.655 --> 01:33:48.702
I had to figure out a way to do it one more time.

2387
01:33:48.702 --> 01:33:50.204
We had to fake celebrate.

2388
01:33:50.204 --> 01:33:51.581
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Fake celebrate

2389
01:33:51.581 --> 01:33:52.789
the whole night.
I knew about it,

2390
01:33:52.789 --> 01:33:54.488
you told me about it, Adam knew about it.

2391
01:33:54.488 --> 01:33:55.992
I mean, I remember-
There was like six people

2392
01:33:55.992 --> 01:33:56.825
that knew about it.
Oh, yeah, Adam,

2393
01:33:56.825 --> 01:33:59.661
'cause Adam would have known.

2394
01:33:59.661 --> 01:34:02.831
Adam and I went down to the finish line

2395
01:34:02.831 --> 01:34:05.206
and we were kind of helping set up and all of that,

2396
01:34:05.206 --> 01:34:07.731
and then Adam got word from Lucy, I think

2397
01:34:07.731 --> 01:34:10.070
like, oh, James is really struggling,

2398
01:34:10.070 --> 01:34:11.331
he's a couple miles out

2399
01:34:11.331 --> 01:34:13.436
and then we jogged up to join the group.

2400
01:34:13.436 --> 01:34:16.716
So I was there, I saw like maybe the last mile

2401
01:34:16.716 --> 01:34:17.648
and a half of that,

2402
01:34:17.648 --> 01:34:20.309
and I was like, oh my God, I don't think he's...

2403
01:34:20.309 --> 01:34:22.920
Like he's so close and it just might not happen.

2404
01:34:22.920 --> 01:34:25.990
And you're like, he's got to do 101 tomorrow.

2405
01:34:25.990 --> 01:34:27.221
I'm like, forget about that,

2406
01:34:27.221 --> 01:34:31.628
let's just get him into the track of the high school.

2407
01:34:31.628 --> 01:34:33.419
And then running around the track,

2408
01:34:33.419 --> 01:34:34.686
like you came back to life

2409
01:34:34.686 --> 01:34:36.793
and you started actually running pretty fast there

2410
01:34:36.793 --> 01:34:37.651
at the end.

2411
01:34:37.651 --> 01:34:40.136
I just couldn't believe like you were literally falling down

2412
01:34:40.136 --> 01:34:40.969
and you couldn't figure out

2413
01:34:40.969 --> 01:34:43.670
how to put your foot on the ground without tripping.

2414
01:34:43.670 --> 01:34:45.518
It's just so crazy the power of the mind

2415
01:34:45.518 --> 01:34:48.273
and when you're so close to something

2416
01:34:48.273 --> 01:34:51.009
and the ability to turn it off.

2417
01:34:51.009 --> 01:34:53.802
Like Casey and Aaron are having a hard time keeping up

2418
01:34:53.802 --> 01:34:55.939
on that last lap 'cause they had done the full thing.

2419
01:34:55.939 --> 01:34:57.621
It was also really hot.
It was hot.

2420
01:34:57.621 --> 01:34:58.637
And neither of them were trained

2421
01:34:58.637 --> 01:35:00.144
for a full distance triathlon

2422
01:35:00.144 --> 01:35:03.742
and Aaron had biked all of those days.

2423
01:35:03.742 --> 01:35:06.067
So Aaron's like I almost couldn't keep up.

2424
01:35:06.067 --> 01:35:07.327
Aaron said, one more half lap

2425
01:35:07.327 --> 01:35:09.340
and I would've fallen over.

2426
01:35:09.340 --> 01:35:11.451
And I just kept praying the entire time,

2427
01:35:11.451 --> 01:35:13.704
I was picking up that pace over the last two laps,

2428
01:35:13.704 --> 01:35:15.217
I was just like, don't fall on your face

2429
01:35:15.217 --> 01:35:16.817
in front of everybody.

2430
01:35:16.817 --> 01:35:20.799
Even though I've been doing it for six miles prior to this,

2431
01:35:20.799 --> 01:35:23.432
but I'm like, you're in the grand stand now

2432
01:35:23.432 --> 01:35:25.265
and every step I took,

2433
01:35:26.484 --> 01:35:27.567
I couldn't believe it,

2434
01:35:27.567 --> 01:35:30.006
I didn't fall over, I didn't fall over, I didn't pull over.

2435
01:35:30.006 --> 01:35:32.965
And I just like kept just saying, stay in your feet,

2436
01:35:32.965 --> 01:35:33.798
stay in your feet,

2437
01:35:33.798 --> 01:35:34.890
stay in your feet.
How cool was that flag

2438
01:35:34.890 --> 01:35:35.723
that you ran under?

2439
01:35:35.723 --> 01:35:36.556
It was really cool.
It was very cool.

2440
01:35:36.556 --> 01:35:38.392
It was a cool moment.
And then 20 minutes later,

2441
01:35:38.392 --> 01:35:41.249
you're up giving a speech, looking fresh as a daisy,

2442
01:35:41.249 --> 01:35:43.608
it's like crazy.
Standing for like 45 minutes

2443
01:35:43.608 --> 01:35:46.431
and I'm like, get the man a chair.

2444
01:35:46.431 --> 01:35:50.367
Well, man, I did pictures for two or three hours.

2445
01:35:50.367 --> 01:35:51.631
You guys were there for a long time.

2446
01:35:51.631 --> 01:35:52.626
Pretending that there was no-

2447
01:35:52.626 --> 01:35:54.906
Two or three hours knowing I'm like,

2448
01:35:54.906 --> 01:35:56.969
okay, I got to get home, I got to get on the therapy table,

2449
01:35:56.969 --> 01:35:58.668
I've got one more day.
So I left at 8:30

2450
01:35:58.668 --> 01:36:01.892
and you had left about 15 or 20 minutes before that,

2451
01:36:01.892 --> 01:36:03.938
so you were out of there by 8:10.

2452
01:36:03.938 --> 01:36:06.252
The 101 just being like the core group,

2453
01:36:06.252 --> 01:36:08.252
like just close friends.

2454
01:36:09.110 --> 01:36:10.865
And that was even special too

2455
01:36:10.865 --> 01:36:12.988
'cause I was planning on just me, Aaron

2456
01:36:12.988 --> 01:36:15.238
and Casey kind of doing it.

2457
01:36:16.832 --> 01:36:18.513
We had celebrated, we had celebrated

2458
01:36:18.513 --> 01:36:22.013
and people probably wanted their rests too

2459
01:36:23.120 --> 01:36:24.574
from the whole thing,

2460
01:36:24.574 --> 01:36:29.143
and Lucy went live every single day on the swim.

2461
01:36:29.143 --> 01:36:30.851
Sunny did.

2462
01:36:30.851 --> 01:36:32.717
Oh yeah, oh yeah, sorry, Sunny did.

2463
01:36:32.717 --> 01:36:34.316
Lucy would push the button.
He lose your partners.

2464
01:36:34.316 --> 01:36:36.782
Lucy would push the button.
Yes,

2465
01:36:36.782 --> 01:36:38.966
and we wanted that moment

2466
01:36:38.966 --> 01:36:42.190
to where it was just me in the pool

2467
01:36:42.190 --> 01:36:43.961
and that's why we didn't tell anybody.

2468
01:36:43.961 --> 01:36:46.711
And I started that swim by myself

2469
01:36:47.920 --> 01:36:49.503
and the chat boards

2470
01:36:50.442 --> 01:36:52.474
and text threads kinda lit up immediately.

2471
01:36:52.474 --> 01:36:54.726
Which we exactly wanted, the element of surprise.

2472
01:36:54.726 --> 01:36:56.001
We wanted that conversation.
With just an instance

2473
01:36:56.001 --> 01:36:57.855
of like, wait a second, he's swimming.

2474
01:36:57.855 --> 01:37:00.475
Is this recovery swim, what's happening?

2475
01:37:00.475 --> 01:37:03.848
And I imagine people thought, oh, he can't sleep

2476
01:37:03.848 --> 01:37:05.524
and he's gonna kind of give a breakdown

2477
01:37:05.524 --> 01:37:07.063
of what happened.
Right,

2478
01:37:07.063 --> 01:37:08.790
this poor guy doesn't know what to do with himself

2479
01:37:08.790 --> 01:37:10.990
so he gotta do it again.

2480
01:37:10.990 --> 01:37:13.534
And then by the time I finished the swim

2481
01:37:13.534 --> 01:37:15.105
and got out of the water,

2482
01:37:15.105 --> 01:37:18.015
the cyclists had got together

2483
01:37:18.015 --> 01:37:19.439
and then started meeting us on the road.

2484
01:37:19.439 --> 01:37:21.769
And then we did an undisclosed run location

2485
01:37:21.769 --> 01:37:23.941
'cause we wanted it to be kind of friends

2486
01:37:23.941 --> 01:37:26.124
and family in core.

2487
01:37:26.124 --> 01:37:27.676
Day 100 was so chaotic,

2488
01:37:27.676 --> 01:37:30.612
it's the opposite of my personality.

2489
01:37:30.612 --> 01:37:33.236
It was so stressful, we had hundreds of riders out there

2490
01:37:33.236 --> 01:37:36.211
and last thing you want to do is crash at high speeds

2491
01:37:36.211 --> 01:37:38.369
on the last day when you're that close,

2492
01:37:38.369 --> 01:37:41.640
and so it was a super stressful bike ride for me,

2493
01:37:41.640 --> 01:37:44.314
and then obviously the excitement and the emotion

2494
01:37:44.314 --> 01:37:47.147
and the stress from that run.

2495
01:37:47.147 --> 01:37:51.048
And so I wanted to kind of go out on my terms

2496
01:37:51.048 --> 01:37:52.880
and the feeling on that day was so different

2497
01:37:52.880 --> 01:37:54.877
'cause we'd accomplished the goal, we did it.

2498
01:37:54.877 --> 01:37:55.828
Yeah,
We did it

2499
01:37:55.828 --> 01:37:59.837
and so that's like the biggest of exhales happened.

2500
01:37:59.837 --> 01:38:02.337
And then it was just this fun,

2501
01:38:03.221 --> 01:38:07.432
chatty core group of cyclists and runners

2502
01:38:07.432 --> 01:38:10.129
that we got to experience and kind of go out on our terms

2503
01:38:10.129 --> 01:38:12.212
and it was a magical day.

2504
01:38:13.281 --> 01:38:16.179
Because you knew you'd finished,

2505
01:38:16.179 --> 01:38:19.802
there's no timeline, there's no expectations,

2506
01:38:19.802 --> 01:38:23.478
it's the ultimate victory lap with your closest team

2507
01:38:23.478 --> 01:38:27.745
and supporters from the past however long.

2508
01:38:27.745 --> 01:38:30.534
But it also sends a very loud and clear message

2509
01:38:30.534 --> 01:38:33.154
that when you've accomplished your goal

2510
01:38:33.154 --> 01:38:37.129
and done the thing you didn't think that you could do,

2511
01:38:37.129 --> 01:38:38.598
you can actually do more.

2512
01:38:38.598 --> 01:38:39.431
Yeah.

2513
01:38:39.431 --> 01:38:42.317
And it just was made undeniable.

2514
01:38:42.317 --> 01:38:46.317
Well I would always get so frustrated speaking

2515
01:38:47.715 --> 01:38:49.854
and someone would always ask after the 50,

2516
01:38:49.854 --> 01:38:51.613
could you have done one more?

2517
01:38:51.613 --> 01:38:53.249
And I was like, they are not gonna ask me

2518
01:38:53.249 --> 01:38:56.249
if I can do one more after this 100.

2519
01:38:57.297 --> 01:38:59.699
And then like we mentioned earlier,

2520
01:38:59.699 --> 01:39:02.539
it was not part of the game plan.

2521
01:39:02.539 --> 01:39:05.711
The week before we started to put it into play

2522
01:39:05.711 --> 01:39:08.080
and Zoka Cycle and Clothing,

2523
01:39:08.080 --> 01:39:11.290
we called her up and we said, hey, we have this idea,

2524
01:39:11.290 --> 01:39:13.463
we know it's in three days, any chance?

2525
01:39:13.463 --> 01:39:15.478
And she's like, send me the logo.

2526
01:39:15.478 --> 01:39:18.299
And her team was planning to drive

2527
01:39:18.299 --> 01:39:19.994
and be at the finish line,

2528
01:39:19.994 --> 01:39:23.892
and they handed that 101 jersey to Lucy

2529
