So you have to almost have a little bit of extra gumption

2781
01:49:55.794 --> 01:49:58.933
to seek it out and put yourself in that situation.

2782
01:49:58.933 --> 01:50:01.892
Sunny always says, and she is not lying when she says it.

2783
01:50:01.892 --> 01:50:03.911
She says, if I have two paths in front of me,

2784
01:50:03.911 --> 01:50:06.073
I'm going to intentionally pick the harder one

2785
01:50:06.073 --> 01:50:11.073
because I wanna struggle, I wanna learn, I wanna grow,

2786
01:50:11.285 --> 01:50:12.732
and that's exact opposite

2787
01:50:12.732 --> 01:50:13.956
of what most people are doing today.

2788
01:50:13.956 --> 01:50:16.400
They see two things and go, that's easy route,

2789
01:50:16.400 --> 01:50:17.573
I'm gonna take that way.

2790
01:50:17.573 --> 01:50:20.577
And that individual, sadly-
It's very unfulfilling.

2791
01:50:20.577 --> 01:50:22.749
It's unfulfilling, they're not gonna grow.

2792
01:50:22.749 --> 01:50:25.548
Like you're diluted into thinking that

2793
01:50:25.548 --> 01:50:27.296
the happy life is the easy life,

2794
01:50:27.296 --> 01:50:29.084
but the happy life, the fulfilled life,

2795
01:50:29.084 --> 01:50:30.307
the purpose driven life

2796
01:50:30.307 --> 01:50:33.983
is the life that invites those sort of difficult situations

2797
01:50:33.983 --> 01:50:35.168
into your experience.
When they're depressed

2798
01:50:35.168 --> 01:50:36.251
and the anxiety and it seems...

2799
01:50:36.251 --> 01:50:37.651
I'm like, I'm sure you do,

2800
01:50:37.651 --> 01:50:40.657
because you're just taking that easy mountain bike path,

2801
01:50:40.657 --> 01:50:43.419
that it's just softer and all you do is...

2802
01:50:43.419 --> 01:50:44.252
There's no challenge,

2803
01:50:44.252 --> 01:50:47.640
there's no reason to develop any character,

2804
01:50:47.640 --> 01:50:49.099
but they're choosing them, right?

2805
01:50:49.099 --> 01:50:51.188
So it's like, well, I'm sure you feel depressed,

2806
01:50:51.188 --> 01:50:53.920
like you're accomplishing nothing hard.

2807
01:50:53.920 --> 01:50:56.729
So that's definitely what our culture

2808
01:50:56.729 --> 01:50:58.516
and our society encourages.

2809
01:50:58.516 --> 01:50:59.802
Yeah.
It's the easy part.

2810
01:50:59.802 --> 01:51:01.023
One of the biggest things you learned

2811
01:51:01.023 --> 01:51:04.773
by taking the harder path is problem solving,

2812
01:51:06.917 --> 01:51:08.366
and that's what our team

2813
01:51:08.366 --> 01:51:12.153
and Sunny has become experts at is problem solving,

2814
01:51:12.153 --> 01:51:12.986
that's all we do.

2815
01:51:12.986 --> 01:51:15.117
We've become master problem solvers

2816
01:51:15.117 --> 01:51:17.103
and we've learned how to problem solve

2817
01:51:17.103 --> 01:51:18.117
in the face of adversity.

2818
01:51:18.117 --> 01:51:20.419
And when you take that path of least resistance,

2819
01:51:20.419 --> 01:51:22.342
there's very limited opportunities

2820
01:51:22.342 --> 01:51:25.098
or necessity to problem solve,

2821
01:51:25.098 --> 01:51:26.682
and so you don't learn that skill set,

2822
01:51:26.682 --> 01:51:29.207
and life is about managing adversity

2823
01:51:29.207 --> 01:51:32.967
and learning how to problem solve at a high level.

2824
01:51:32.967 --> 01:51:33.925
Under stressful circumstances.

2825
01:51:33.925 --> 01:51:35.057
Under stressful circumstances.

2826
01:51:35.057 --> 01:51:36.015
You're not problem solving.
So the problem

2827
01:51:36.015 --> 01:51:37.802
for you being overwhelmed

2828
01:51:37.802 --> 01:51:39.268
is probably really high.

2829
01:51:39.268 --> 01:51:40.293
Oh, yeah.

2830
01:51:40.293 --> 01:51:42.172
Like nothing's a big deal.

2831
01:51:42.172 --> 01:51:45.083
No, no, I'll just, I'll figure it out.

2832
01:51:45.083 --> 01:51:46.410
And I mean, that was the whole journey

2833
01:51:46.410 --> 01:51:51.410
of the 100 was adaptation, nothing was ever the same.

2834
01:51:51.427 --> 01:51:54.094
Every day, the mood, the injury,

2835
01:51:55.432 --> 01:52:00.268
the fatigue of the crew or James, the food he wanted,

2836
01:52:00.268 --> 01:52:03.020
the people that were showing up, the weather.

2837
01:52:03.020 --> 01:52:05.587
I mean every day was adaptation.

2838
01:52:05.587 --> 01:52:08.520
And I remember being late in the journey going,

2839
01:52:08.520 --> 01:52:13.520
man, we're in 90 days in, and nothing's ever the same.

2840
01:52:13.791 --> 01:52:15.175
You grocery shop for the week

2841
01:52:15.175 --> 01:52:17.621
and James doesn't want anything you buy,

2842
01:52:17.621 --> 01:52:20.264
and it's literally minute to minute to minute.

2843
01:52:20.264 --> 01:52:25.216
So I don't have a lot of tolerance for people who say,

2844
01:52:25.216 --> 01:52:26.499
it's just hard, I don't have the resources,

2845
01:52:26.499 --> 01:52:27.693
I can't figure it out.

2846
01:52:27.693 --> 01:52:29.473
And I'm like, dude, you just figure it out,

2847
01:52:29.473 --> 01:52:30.363
that's life, you just figure out,

2848
01:52:30.363 --> 01:52:32.027
nobody has the instruction manual,

2849
01:52:32.027 --> 01:52:34.749
nobody knows what they're doing, you just figure it out,

2850
01:52:34.749 --> 01:52:37.731
and a lot of times you don't have the time to figure it out.

2851
01:52:37.731 --> 01:52:39.625
You have like 10 seconds

2852
01:52:39.625 --> 01:52:43.141
to figure out a solution right here right now, I mean.

2853
01:52:43.141 --> 01:52:44.347
And that was the premise of the 100

2854
01:52:44.347 --> 01:52:47.052
was remove the chaos, put in normality,

2855
01:52:47.052 --> 01:52:48.891
put in consistency.
Create illusion.

2856
01:52:48.891 --> 01:52:51.091
Remove the chaos.
Good luck with that.

2857
01:52:51.091 --> 01:52:51.924
One of those things

2858
01:52:51.924 --> 01:52:53.883
that we thought we were gonna able to control

2859
01:52:53.883 --> 01:52:57.100
and ultimately it became-
It was exactly the same.

2860
01:52:57.100 --> 01:53:00.351
It became chaotic as the 50, but for twice as long.

2861
01:53:00.351 --> 01:53:01.979
Exactly the same, but different.

2862
01:53:01.979 --> 01:53:04.486
I mean, it was just as chaotic,

2863
01:53:04.486 --> 01:53:07.536
just as necessary to solve problems,

2864
01:53:07.536 --> 01:53:10.528
just as dramatic, just different.

2865
01:53:10.528 --> 01:53:14.120
It was unbelievably exactly the same

2866
01:53:14.120 --> 01:53:15.585
as far as emotions and stress.

2867
01:53:15.585 --> 01:53:17.236
What's a story that hasn't been told

2868
01:53:17.236 --> 01:53:20.719
like a behind the scenes, what do people not get

2869
01:53:20.719 --> 01:53:25.521
or not understand about how this whole thing unfolded?

2870
01:53:25.521 --> 01:53:29.685
From both perspectives, James what's yours?

2871
01:53:29.685 --> 01:53:31.791
I think, man, that's a great question,

2872
01:53:31.791 --> 01:53:33.928
I've never been asked that before.

2873
01:53:33.928 --> 01:53:34.901
You're a winner

2874
01:53:34.901 --> 01:53:36.077
'cause he gets asked a lot of the same questions.

2875
01:53:36.077 --> 01:53:37.335
I do this for a living.

2876
01:53:37.335 --> 01:53:39.336
That's pretty good.
This is my job.

2877
01:53:39.336 --> 01:53:43.503
Most people ask the same questions, you got him.

2878
01:53:46.122 --> 01:53:46.955
Gosh.

2879
01:53:50.226 --> 01:53:52.040
I will say this, few people will ever understand

2880
01:53:52.040 --> 01:53:55.334
what it takes and what the four of us went through,

2881
01:53:55.334 --> 01:54:00.065
even if you've read every book, seen every interview.

2882
01:54:00.065 --> 01:54:02.779
I mean it had to put a strain on your marriage?

2883
01:54:02.779 --> 01:54:03.891
No.
No?

2884
01:54:03.891 --> 01:54:06.724
Well...
Maybe his but not mine.

2885
01:54:07.587 --> 01:54:08.647
He's like, well I don't know,

2886
01:54:08.647 --> 01:54:10.869
actually was out there riding my bike.

2887
01:54:10.869 --> 01:54:13.036
No.
Even I didn't know.

2888
01:54:16.548 --> 01:54:19.689
I think Sunny is actually super mature

2889
01:54:19.689 --> 01:54:23.643
and one of the biggest size of relief for me when she says,

2890
01:54:23.643 --> 01:54:26.618
I just gave you 100 day pass on anything you said

2891
01:54:26.618 --> 01:54:27.654
and anything you did,

2892
01:54:27.654 --> 01:54:30.988
and I'm like, no other woman on the planet does that.

2893
01:54:30.988 --> 01:54:33.113
But just her level of understanding of,

2894
01:54:33.113 --> 01:54:35.651
okay, look, this isn't my husband

2895
01:54:35.651 --> 01:54:37.751
and there's an imbalance,

2896
01:54:37.751 --> 01:54:39.333
there's a hormonal thing going on,

2897
01:54:39.333 --> 01:54:41.458
there's a stress thing going on,

2898
01:54:41.458 --> 01:54:44.041
this is totally situational,

2899
01:54:44.041 --> 01:54:47.374
and thankfully I did get a 100 day pass.

2900
01:54:50.730 --> 01:54:51.811
I don't think people realize

2901
01:54:51.811 --> 01:54:55.031
that it was literally second to second.

2902
01:54:55.031 --> 01:54:57.341
I mean, and I don't know if that was everybody's experience,

2903
01:54:57.341 --> 01:54:58.716
but that was certainly mine.

2904
01:54:58.716 --> 01:55:01.767
I mean, from the second I got up

2905
01:55:01.767 --> 01:55:04.589
until I was climbing into bed,

2906
01:55:04.589 --> 01:55:07.570
knowing I was only getting two hours of sleep,

2907
01:55:07.570 --> 01:55:11.403
every second was high intensity and demanding.

2908
01:55:12.730 --> 01:55:15.063
I mean, there was no refuge.

2909
01:55:16.414 --> 01:55:20.664
So that I think about people in their own struggles

2910
01:55:21.868 --> 01:55:23.598
and there's a lot of times you're like,

2911
01:55:23.598 --> 01:55:27.534
okay, I'm gonna go in my closet and take five breaths.

2912
01:55:27.534 --> 01:55:30.652
Like that didn't exist for me because I had my family,

2913
01:55:30.652 --> 01:55:33.338
I had the crew, I had James,

2914
01:55:33.338 --> 01:55:36.511
I mean the film crew, James, I had our working crew,

2915
01:55:36.511 --> 01:55:38.142
I had the volunteer church stuff

2916
01:55:38.142 --> 01:55:39.810
I was doing in the community,

2917
01:55:39.810 --> 01:55:43.304
my parents live in my basement, we have two dogs.

2918
01:55:43.304 --> 01:55:44.863
I mean, there was literally...

2919
01:55:44.863 --> 01:55:47.498
A lot of people whose needs need to be met,

2920
01:55:47.498 --> 01:55:49.605
who are looking to you to meet those needs,

2921
01:55:49.605 --> 01:55:52.183
and not a lot of time for Sunny to meet Sunny's needs.

2922
01:55:52.183 --> 01:55:54.502
Which I knew was only temporary, so it was okay.

2923
01:55:54.502 --> 01:55:57.731
But 100 days is long, temporary phase.

2924
01:55:57.731 --> 01:55:59.008
Yeah, and it took me about two years

2925
01:55:59.008 --> 01:56:02.341
to recover from the 50, and so I promised myself this time,

2926
01:56:02.341 --> 01:56:04.676
along the way, I would do things

2927
01:56:04.676 --> 01:56:08.114
to prevent needing that much time to recover.

2928
01:56:08.114 --> 01:56:09.609
And so that's why now I'm like,

2929
01:56:09.609 --> 01:56:12.781
there's definitely still some PTSD that I have to process

2930
01:56:12.781 --> 01:56:14.562
that I just haven't had the chance to yet

2931
01:56:14.562 --> 01:56:16.290
and I've just started that.

2932
01:56:16.290 --> 01:56:19.670
So I definitely feel better than coming off the 50,

2933
01:56:19.670 --> 01:56:22.337
but it was intense every second.

2934
01:56:24.267 --> 01:56:27.786
Yeah, it's kind of like an extrapolated version of

2935
01:56:27.786 --> 01:56:30.895
when somebody goes into crew, like an ultra race

2936
01:56:30.895 --> 01:56:32.165
and they've never crewed before

2937
01:56:32.165 --> 01:56:33.554
and they think they're just gonna be in a van,

2938
01:56:33.554 --> 01:56:36.710
listening to music and it's gonna be super cool and chill.

2939
01:56:36.710 --> 01:56:38.293
And they're like, wait,

2940
01:56:38.293 --> 01:56:40.069
they're doing stuff all the like...

2941
01:56:40.069 --> 01:56:43.586
But that's times 1000 for 100 days straight.

2942
01:56:43.586 --> 01:56:44.419
Yeah.

2943
01:56:44.419 --> 01:56:47.150
I think the stories that haven't been told yet,

2944
01:56:47.150 --> 01:56:48.624
or the stories that we don't know yet

2945
01:56:48.624 --> 01:56:50.914
of the people we've impacted,

2946
01:56:50.914 --> 01:56:52.880
I think that's the biggest thing.

2947
01:56:52.880 --> 01:56:56.317
They are yet to come.
That are yet to come.

2948
01:56:56.317 --> 01:56:58.367
And those are obviously the most meaningful stories

2949
01:56:58.367 --> 01:57:01.690
and a lot of them we won't ever get to hear.

2950
01:57:01.690 --> 01:57:04.971
Back on the mental toughness piece,

2951
01:57:04.971 --> 01:57:05.951
you had mentioned something

2952
01:57:05.951 --> 01:57:08.482
that's a little bit tangential to it,

2953
01:57:08.482 --> 01:57:10.688
which is this idea of showing up, right?

2954
01:57:10.688 --> 01:57:13.351
The idea of being consistent

2955
01:57:13.351 --> 01:57:16.905
and how that plays into long-term success

2956
01:57:16.905 --> 01:57:20.345
and the truth being that it's not sexy

2957
01:57:20.345 --> 01:57:21.375
and it's not something

2958
01:57:21.375 --> 01:57:23.382
that trends in social media,

2959
01:57:23.382 --> 01:57:24.278
it's like that stuff

2960
01:57:24.278 --> 01:57:26.512
that you do every single day, no matter what

2961
01:57:26.512 --> 01:57:30.202
that moves the needle forward, ever so slightly,

2962
01:57:30.202 --> 01:57:33.508
that puts you in the position to be able to do great things

2963
01:57:33.508 --> 01:57:35.319
and achieve your dreams.

2964
01:57:35.319 --> 01:57:38.445
I got to have a really cool experience.

2965
01:57:38.445 --> 01:57:41.293
I've had the opportunity to speak to some NFL teams

2966
01:57:41.293 --> 01:57:44.983
and I was on the field for a warmup for one of the games

2967
01:57:44.983 --> 01:57:47.966
and one of the coach was there talking to me

2968
01:57:47.966 --> 01:57:51.897
and the quarterback was throwing the ball

2969
01:57:51.897 --> 01:57:53.828
to a couple of different receivers

2970
01:57:53.828 --> 01:57:55.204
and he said, watch this.

2971
01:57:55.204 --> 01:57:57.271
And he threw the ball and the receiver caught it

2972
01:57:57.271 --> 01:57:59.801
and immediately tucked it and then drop the ball,

2973
01:57:59.801 --> 01:58:01.597
caught the next one and immediately tucked it.

2974
01:58:01.597 --> 01:58:04.125
And then he started throwing the ball to a newer member

2975
01:58:04.125 --> 01:58:05.372
of the team where were rookie

2976
01:58:05.372 --> 01:58:08.497
and he would catch it and drop it, catch it and drop it

2977
01:58:08.497 --> 01:58:11.923
and he said, he's not gonna make it in this league.

2978
01:58:11.923 --> 01:58:14.000
And the reason he's a successful veteran

2979
01:58:14.000 --> 01:58:17.390
is because he's still doing the small things

2980
01:58:17.390 --> 01:58:19.157
and working on the fundamentals

2981
01:58:19.157 --> 01:58:22.016
that you would think they would take for granted

2982
01:58:22.016 --> 01:58:23.647
over not put much attention to it,

2983
01:58:23.647 --> 01:58:25.533
but the fact that it would catch it and still tuck it,

2984
01:58:25.533 --> 01:58:28.843
like it was in a game situation where he was protecting it,

2985
01:58:28.843 --> 01:58:32.343
even in just tossing a ball to you, right?

2986
01:58:33.206 --> 01:58:34.039
That type of thing.

2987
01:58:34.039 --> 01:58:35.189
The coaches watch that kind of stuff

2988
01:58:35.189 --> 01:58:37.487
and it's that level of consistency,

2989
01:58:37.487 --> 01:58:38.593
it's that level of showing up,

2990
01:58:38.593 --> 01:58:42.374
it's that level of doing the small things

2991
01:58:42.374 --> 01:58:45.552
over a long period of time that people aren't willing to do

2992
01:58:45.552 --> 01:58:48.534
that separates that guy who makes it

2993
01:58:48.534 --> 01:58:51.011
and that guy who ultimately will get cut.

2994
01:58:51.011 --> 01:58:52.344
Yeah, so true.

2995
01:58:56.934 --> 01:58:59.421
How does it work with balance?

2996
01:58:59.421 --> 01:59:01.860
I'm sure you get that question a lot too.

2997
01:59:01.860 --> 01:59:03.378
He does get that one a lot.
Yeah.

2998
01:59:03.378 --> 01:59:05.657
Your life's totally out of balance, dude.

2999
01:59:05.657 --> 01:59:06.974
No, it's not.

3000
01:59:06.974 --> 01:59:08.432
Well, you're guy with...

3001
01:59:08.432 --> 01:59:10.093
You have four kids, right?
Yeah.

3002
01:59:10.093 --> 01:59:12.543
So I'm sure you get that question a lot too, right?

3003
01:59:12.543 --> 01:59:13.376
I do.

3004
01:59:14.626 --> 01:59:18.257
My answer evolves, but I have kind of a response to that,

3005
01:59:18.257 --> 01:59:19.919
but I'm interested in how you guys think about that.

3006
01:59:19.919 --> 01:59:21.767
My answers have evolved too

3007
01:59:21.767 --> 01:59:25.169
and now that I have four teenage girls.

3008
01:59:25.169 --> 01:59:26.842
So fun.
It is fun,

3009
01:59:26.842 --> 01:59:29.622
but this is the example that I use.

3010
01:59:29.622 --> 01:59:34.622
My 13 year old daughter doesn't want like 25% of my time.

3011
01:59:35.071 --> 01:59:36.323
'Cause people like assume,

3012
01:59:36.323 --> 01:59:37.371
oh, family life balance.
You're lucky

3013
01:59:37.371 --> 01:59:38.554
if you get 5 minutes.

3014
01:59:38.554 --> 01:59:40.166
Well, yeah and people assume,

3015
01:59:40.166 --> 01:59:44.552
okay, let's say, let's break life into work, play, family.

3016
01:59:44.552 --> 01:59:47.302
And if balance equals 33, 33, 33,

3017
01:59:48.802 --> 01:59:50.784
then you've got to give that amount of time

3018
01:59:50.784 --> 01:59:52.280
to each one of those.

3019
01:59:52.280 --> 01:59:53.839
And that's the best example

3020
01:59:53.839 --> 01:59:57.638
is my daughter doesn't want 33% of my time,

3021
01:59:57.638 --> 01:59:58.512
that's absurd.

3022
01:59:58.512 --> 02:00:02.074
What she does want is when I am getting over my time,

3023
02:00:02.074 --> 02:00:03.793
she wants all of my time,

3024
02:00:03.793 --> 02:00:06.931
and she wants me to be right there, attentive,

3025
02:00:06.931 --> 02:00:08.197
listening to the story

3026
02:00:08.197 --> 02:00:12.295
that I don't necessarily all the details care about.

3027
02:00:12.295 --> 02:00:15.036
But I mean, we've got one daughter who Sunny will say,

3028
02:00:15.036 --> 02:00:15.869
how was your day?

3029
02:00:15.869 --> 02:00:18.009
And literally from when she woke up to when-

3030
02:00:18.009 --> 02:00:20.520
I woke up and I did this and then this

3031
02:00:20.520 --> 02:00:21.418
and its like...

3032
02:00:21.418 --> 02:00:22.301
Oh, the whole time?

3033
02:00:22.301 --> 02:00:23.375
I see, I would kill for that,

3034
02:00:23.375 --> 02:00:24.977
I get a lot of like fine

3035
02:00:24.977 --> 02:00:25.810
and that's all I get.
Yeah, we have one

3036
02:00:25.810 --> 02:00:26.643
of those too, how was your day?

3037
02:00:26.643 --> 02:00:27.476
"Fine," anything happened?

3038
02:00:27.476 --> 02:00:29.299
"No."
Yeah, but family life

3039
02:00:29.299 --> 02:00:31.800
and work balance doesn't mean an equal percentage,

3040
02:00:31.800 --> 02:00:36.022
it means whatever you're doing, give that balance to it.

3041
02:00:36.022 --> 02:00:40.772
And the 100 is a perfect example, totally out of balance,

3042
02:00:42.163 --> 02:00:44.746
but that imbalance is temporary

3043
02:00:46.278 --> 02:00:48.930
and the sacrifices were discussed with the families.

3044
02:00:48.930 --> 02:00:50.748
Everybody was committed to the imbalance

3045
02:00:50.748 --> 02:00:52.512
including the kids.
Okay, okay,

3046
02:00:52.512 --> 02:00:54.115
life's gonna be completely out of bounds

3047
02:00:54.115 --> 02:00:57.100
for a while, and it will shift back to imbalance.

3048
02:00:57.100 --> 02:00:59.394
And to break through barriers

3049
02:00:59.394 --> 02:01:01.547
and to reach certain levels and whatnot,

3050
02:01:01.547 --> 02:01:03.125
there has to be some...

3051
02:01:03.125 --> 02:01:06.464
Nobody that navigates this life successfully

3052
02:01:06.464 --> 02:01:08.157
has a perfect balance at all times.

3053
02:01:08.157 --> 02:01:09.969
Now what you have to be careful of

3054
02:01:09.969 --> 02:01:11.499
is going completely out of balance

3055
02:01:11.499 --> 02:01:13.548
for a really long period of time.

3056
02:01:13.548 --> 02:01:17.394
Now you're jeopardizing and creating problems.

3057
02:01:17.394 --> 02:01:20.597
What's your thoughts on balance?

3058
02:01:20.597 --> 02:01:23.094
I think that balance is ebb and flow,

3059
02:01:23.094 --> 02:01:25.323
it's like a marriage is never 50, 50,

3060
02:01:25.323 --> 02:01:27.809
sometimes it's 60, 40, sometimes it's 70, 30,

3061
02:01:27.809 --> 02:01:30.966
depending on which partner needs more attention at the time.

3062
02:01:30.966 --> 02:01:32.399
I think life is like that,

3063
02:01:32.399 --> 02:01:36.036
sometimes you don't need downtime, you need uptime.

3064
02:01:36.036 --> 02:01:38.402
You don't need to rest, you need to be more exhilarated

3065
02:01:38.402 --> 02:01:40.114
to have more passion.

3066
02:01:40.114 --> 02:01:43.641
So I think the appropriate thing with balance is gauging

3067
02:01:43.641 --> 02:01:45.742
where you're at personally, where your family's at,

3068
02:01:45.742 --> 02:01:48.479
what your goals are, what the demands are

3069
02:01:48.479 --> 02:01:50.468
and doing so accordingly,

3070
02:01:50.468 --> 02:01:53.606
because like you said, it evolves, right?

3071
02:01:53.606 --> 02:01:54.842
It changes over time.

3072
02:01:54.842 --> 02:01:56.681
Look, if you're writing a book,

3073
02:01:56.681 --> 02:01:58.475
your time balance is gonna be different

3074
02:01:58.475 --> 02:01:59.618
than when the book's complete

3075
02:01:59.618 --> 02:02:00.721
and your marketing the book.

3076
02:02:00.721 --> 02:02:02.223
Right.
Now your time and attention

3077
02:02:02.223 --> 02:02:03.900
is gonna go somewhere else

3078
02:02:03.900 --> 02:02:05.098
but it's the same project,

3079
02:02:05.098 --> 02:02:06.647
you're trying to accomplish the same goal,

3080
02:02:06.647 --> 02:02:08.463
but it has to sacrifice differently

3081
02:02:08.463 --> 02:02:09.937
to get to the end of that project.

3082
02:02:09.937 --> 02:02:10.962
Reviewing your activity level,

3083
02:02:10.962 --> 02:02:13.492
you're like I'm going to be sitting a lot more in the day

3084
02:02:13.492 --> 02:02:14.904
than if I'm working on my garden.

3085
02:02:14.904 --> 02:02:16.615
Yeah, I mean, it's a tricky thing.

3086
02:02:16.615 --> 02:02:17.448
I mean,

3087
02:02:19.980 --> 02:02:22.151 line:15%
I think culture dictates this idea

3088
02:02:22.151 --> 02:02:25.669 line:15%
that we should be aspiring to live our life

3089
02:02:25.669 --> 02:02:27.752 line:15%
in this super balanced way every single day

3090
02:02:27.752 --> 02:02:30.755 line:15%
and that our time and attention is equally apportioned

3091
02:02:30.755 --> 02:02:32.124
throughout the hours of the day

3092
02:02:32.124 --> 02:02:33.583
so that everybody's taken care of

3093
02:02:33.583 --> 02:02:34.990
and you're taking care of yourself

3094
02:02:34.990 --> 02:02:37.701
and it sets people up for failure and for guilt,

3095
02:02:37.701 --> 02:02:39.345
like we beat ourselves up

3096
02:02:39.345 --> 02:02:41.314
because we're not adhering to that kind of norm

3097
02:02:41.314 --> 02:02:42.891
and that norm is an illusion.

3098
02:02:42.891 --> 02:02:44.090
I don't think anybody adheres

3099
02:02:44.090 --> 02:02:46.004
to that norm successfully.

3100
02:02:46.004 --> 02:02:49.724
And on top of that, if you wanna do something amazing,

3101
02:02:49.724 --> 02:02:52.872
your life is gonna have to look unlike other people's lives.

3102
02:02:52.872 --> 02:02:54.823
I mean, that's just the truth,

3103
02:02:54.823 --> 02:02:56.398
nobody achieves something great

3104
02:02:56.398 --> 02:02:58.437
with some perfectly balanced life,

3105
02:02:58.437 --> 02:03:00.545
you have to be temporarily out of balance

3106
02:03:00.545 --> 02:03:03.364
so that something gets an extraordinary amount of time,

3107
02:03:03.364 --> 02:03:05.262
attention and focus.
It's your peaking period,

3108
02:03:05.262 --> 02:03:06.095
your peaking.

3109
02:03:06.095 --> 02:03:07.202
I think of it as a pendulum

3110
02:03:07.202 --> 02:03:08.847
and that pendulum has to swing back.

3111
02:03:08.847 --> 02:03:10.245
Like you have to make sure

3112
02:03:10.245 --> 02:03:12.600
that the important buckets in your life

3113
02:03:12.600 --> 02:03:14.367
are being attended to,

3114
02:03:14.367 --> 02:03:17.397
so that you don't capsize completely,

3115
02:03:17.397 --> 02:03:19.895
but you have to be in a situation

3116
02:03:19.895 --> 02:03:23.184
where you can kind of vacillate in and out of these things.

3117
02:03:23.184 --> 02:03:24.086
And that's okay,

3118
02:03:24.086 --> 02:03:26.690
as long as it always kind of like tips back

3119
02:03:26.690 --> 02:03:27.791
in the right direction.

3120
02:03:27.791 --> 02:03:28.767
Yeah, beautiful said.

3121
02:03:28.767 --> 02:03:30.350
And don't you think that people know

3122
02:03:30.350 --> 02:03:32.183
when their life is out of balance?

3123
02:03:32.183 --> 02:03:34.137
Sure.
'Cause either you're sad

3124
02:03:34.137 --> 02:03:36.741
or you're too tired or you're this or that

3125
02:03:36.741 --> 02:03:38.016
and then you assess, right?

3126
02:03:38.016 --> 02:03:40.194
Well our bodies are amazing too, they give us signals.

3127
02:03:40.194 --> 02:03:41.777
Yeah and I think,

3128
02:03:42.640 --> 02:03:44.763
I like to think of it more in terms of attention,

3129
02:03:44.763 --> 02:03:46.395
like where are you placing your attention

3130
02:03:46.395 --> 02:03:48.645
and is that the right place to be placing your attention?

3131
02:03:48.645 --> 02:03:50.518
And when you're placing your attention on that thing,

3132
02:03:50.518 --> 02:03:53.706
are you giving it all that you have

3133
02:03:53.706 --> 02:03:57.297
and you can pull out of it and then rejigger

3134
02:03:57.297 --> 02:03:59.170
and focus it somewhere else,

3135
02:03:59.170 --> 02:04:00.888
but being present for what you're doing.

3136
02:04:00.888 --> 02:04:04.796
And I think, a big piece of like the lesson that I extract,

3137
02:04:04.796 --> 02:04:07.200
one of the lessons I extract from the 100

3138
02:04:07.200 --> 02:04:08.469
is this mindfulness piece.

3139
02:04:08.469 --> 02:04:10.882
Like this idea of being totally present

3140
02:04:10.882 --> 02:04:14.030
with what you're doing, it's too overwhelming, right?

3141
02:04:14.030 --> 02:04:16.722
The only way that you got through it

3142
02:04:16.722 --> 02:04:20.608
is by being exactly where your feet were,

3143
02:04:20.608 --> 02:04:24.191
every second of every mile of every day.

3144
02:04:24.191 --> 02:04:26.644
Yeah, as soon as I looked too far ahead,

3145
02:04:26.644 --> 02:04:28.146
it was catastrophic.

3146
02:04:28.146 --> 02:04:30.116
Well, and you couldn't have balance.

3147
02:04:30.116 --> 02:04:31.322
He had one job.

3148
02:04:31.322 --> 02:04:34.400
Yeah.
Swim, bike, and run.

3149
02:04:34.400 --> 02:04:35.761
That was it.

3150
02:04:35.761 --> 02:04:39.552
If he tried to implement anything else, like you said,

3151
02:04:39.552 --> 02:04:40.900
he couldn't have accomplished it,

3152
02:04:40.900 --> 02:04:42.167
it couldn't have happened, right?

3153
02:04:42.167 --> 02:04:45.171
So, yeah, that was out of balance

3154
02:04:45.171 --> 02:04:47.747
but the appropriate thing to do

3155
02:04:47.747 --> 02:04:51.080
is to immediately balance out your time,

3156
02:04:52.148 --> 02:04:55.006
efforts and energies, as soon as that project is done,

3157
02:04:55.006 --> 02:04:56.675
and I think that's where people struggle.

3158
02:04:56.675 --> 02:04:59.095
I think they try to continue what they're doing,

3159
02:04:59.095 --> 02:05:00.426
they don't recover after a race,

3160
02:05:00.426 --> 02:05:02.428
they just continue their training,

3161
02:05:02.428 --> 02:05:04.457
but I think you articulated that beautifully.

3162
02:05:04.457 --> 02:05:05.644
Yeah.
And here, sorry,

3163
02:05:05.644 --> 02:05:09.385
here's a great example of, I sacrificed a lot of family time

3164
02:05:09.385 --> 02:05:11.206
during those 100 years-

3165
02:05:11.206 --> 02:05:13.608
100 years, that is what it felt like.

